        ],
        "notes": "A visa is required, according to the Australian Government, which says to obtain it before you enter the DRC; you can't get one on arrival. Apply for the official eVisa (evisa.gouv.cd), accepted at any DRC entry point: it entitles you to a 7-day, extendable airport visa (VAP, USD 90 at the port of entry). Or obtain a visa from a DRC embassy before travel. The eVisa is the \"visa volant\": the immigration service’s eVisa FAQ lists its types as the specific, ordinary and family-visit visa volant.",
