      "cashImportance": "high",
      "text": "The UK says credit cards are accepted only in a limited number of places in Kinshasa and other cities, that US dollars are widely used alongside the Congolese franc, and that cash is needed elsewhere. Canada describes a cash-based economy and says shopkeepers and exchange dealers require undamaged, recent dollar notes printed after 2009."
    },
    "safety": {
      "level": "high-risk",
      "text": "Canada advises against all travel to the DRC, citing the fragile security situation and an Ebola outbreak. The UK advises against all travel to North Kivu, South Kivu, Ituri, Haut-Uélé, Maniema, Tanganyika and Haut-Lomami provinces, the Kwamouth territory of Mai-Ndombe and within 50 km of the Central African Republic border. It says armed groups are active in eastern DRC, where M23 rebels have captured Goma and Bukavu. In Kinshasa, Lubumbashi and other cities the UK says foreign nationals are at particular risk of street robbery.",
      "source": {
