  "faq": [
    {
      "id": "need-visa",
      "question": "Do I need a visa for the Democratic Republic of the Congo?",
      "answer": "The UK, Canadian, Australian and Italian governments say their citizens need a visa, obtained before travel. The immigration service's eVisa (evisa.gouv.cd), the \"visa volant\", is open to any foreigner visiting for tourism, and DRC embassies also issue visas. No official source we could read states which other nationalities need a visa, and the immigration service publishes no list of visa-exempt nationalities."
    },
    {
      "id": "evisa-how",
      "question": "How does the DRC eVisa work?",
      "answer": "Apply on the official portal, evisa.gouv.cd. The immigration service (DGM) says the eVisa can be used at any DRC entry point, by air, land, sea or lake; it must be used within three months of issue and entitles you to a single-entry, 7-day extendable airport visa (VAP), which costs USD 90 at the border."
    },
    {
      "id": "visa-volant",
      "question": "What is the \"visa volant\"?",
      "answer": "It is the DRC eVisa. The immigration service’s eVisa FAQ lists the eVisa’s types as the specific visa volant, the ordinary visa volant and the visa volant for family visits. You apply on evisa.gouv.cd (USD 300) and receive a 7-day extendable airport visa (VAP, USD 90) at the port of entry."
    },
    {
      "id": "yellow-fever",
      "question": "Is the yellow fever vaccine mandatory for the DRC?",
      "answer": "Yes. The UK government says you must have a yellow fever vaccination certificate to enter the DRC."
    },
    {
      "id": "safety",
      "question": "Is the DRC safe to visit?",
      "answer": "Canada advises against all travel to the DRC, and the UK advises against all travel to parts of the east, including North Kivu and Ituri. Canada says armed groups control Goma and Bukavu, and that violent demonstrations, sometimes targeting foreign nationals, have taken place in Kinshasa."
    },
    {
      "id": "eac",
      "question": "Do East African Community citizens need a visa for the DRC?",
      "answer": "No official DRC source we could find publishes a visa exemption for EAC citizens: the immigration service’s eVisa FAQ names none."
    }
  ]
